Spring creates proxy objects
Method calls resolved dynamically
Proxy types:
  JDK Proxy → interface-based
  CGLIB → class-based (uses inheritance)

17. Common Tricky Interview Questions (4+ Years)
Q1. Can constructors be polymorphic?
❌ No — constructors are not inherited.

Q2. Can private methods be overridden?
❌ No — not visible to child.

Q3. Can polymorphism work without inheritance?
✅ Yes — using interfaces.

Q4. Why final methods block polymorphism?
Because overriding is not allowed.

Q5. Is polymorphism compile-time or runtime?
✔ Both:
Overloading → Compile-time
Overriding → Runtime

